---
title Diagrama de classes (1/2) — Domínio: leads, vendedores, atribuição, deduplicação e rastreabilidade
---
classDiagram
  direction LR

  class Seller {
    +string id
    +string name
    +string email  «único»
    +boolean active
    +Date lastAssignedAt  «ponteiro do round-robin»
    +Date createdAt
    +Date updatedAt
  }

  class Lead {
    +string id  «UUID público»
    +number seq  «interno, só paginação»
    +string name
    +string email
    +string phone  «E.164 — chave de deduplicação, único»
    +Channel channel
    +string origin
    +string notes
    +LeadStatus status
    +string sellerId
    +Date assignedAt
    +Date createdAt
  }

  class LeadEvent {
    +number seq
    +string leadId
    +LeadEventType type
    +EventChannel channel
    +string sellerId
    +string webhookEventId
    +string requestId
    +Map metadata
    +Date createdAt
  }

  class WebhookEvent {
    +string id
    +string source
    +string externalEventId  «único com source»
    +WebhookEnvelope payload
    +string payloadHash
    +WebhookStatus status
    +number attempts
    +Date nextAttemptAt
    +Date enqueuedAt
    +Date lockedUntil
    +string lastError
    +string leadId
    +Date receivedAt
    +Date processedAt
  }

  class CreateLeadInput {
    +string name
    +string phone
    +string email
    +string origin
    +string notes
  }

  class WebhookEnvelope {
    +string event_id
    +string source
    +CreateLeadInput data
  }

  class LeadStatus {
    <<enumeration>>
    unassigned
    assigned
  }
  class Channel {
    <<enumeration>>
    api
    webhook
  }
  class LeadEventType {
    <<enumeration>>
    lead.created
    lead.assigned
    lead.duplicate_attempt
  }
  class WebhookStatus {
    <<enumeration>>
    pending
    processing
    processed
    duplicate
    dead
  }

  Seller "0..1" <-- "0..*" Lead : atendido por (seller_id)
  Lead "1" *-- "1..*" LeadEvent : rastreia (append-only)
  Seller "0..1" <-- "0..*" LeadEvent : atribuído a
  WebhookEvent "0..1" <-- "0..*" LeadEvent : originado por
  WebhookEvent "0..*" --> "0..1" Lead : gerou ou duplicou
  WebhookEnvelope "1" *-- "1" CreateLeadInput : data
  WebhookEvent "1" *-- "1" WebhookEnvelope : payload
  Lead ..> LeadStatus
  Lead ..> Channel
  LeadEvent ..> LeadEventType
  WebhookEvent ..> WebhookStatus

  note for Lead "Invariante (CHECK no MySQL): unassigned ⇒ sem vendedor e sem assigned_at; assigned ⇒ com vendedor e assigned_at. UNIQUE(phone_e164) impede duplicidade mesmo sob concorrência"
  note for LeadEvent "Cada lead tem ao menos 'lead.created'; 'lead.assigned' quando recebe vendedor; 'lead.duplicate_attempt' a cada tentativa repetida"
